# CHEM-JCTC-060: Entropic Collapse Model of Molecular Stability

## Overview

This paper presents a novel theoretical framework for predicting molecular stability based on a self-referential entropic collapse principle. Rather than relying on traditional thermodynamic parameters like ΔG and ΔS, we introduce "collapse entropy" (Ε_collapse) as a fundamental measure derived directly from molecular structure. This approach enables stability predictions without requiring empirical data input.

